# 📡️ REAL binary diff frame. Ticket 26/08/10/ARTIFACT-SYSTEM-OVERHAUL-REAL-CODECS-RUNTIME-REUSE-EVOLUTION:
# this standard had NO `DiffCodec` impl at all before this wave (not even F6's `print_diff().into_bytes()`
# text-as-binary shortcut — the sole remaining `dsl-migration/diff-completeness` breach across all 32
# stdio standards) — replaces the old ABNF placeholder this file used to contain. Same structural
# reasoning as the sibling `../../🧬️mutations/💾️binary/📡️component.protocol.semio` (read that file's
# comment for the full `DslField`/recursion rationale — it applies identically here, `Part21Value`'s
# self-recursive `List`/`Typed` case is the same recursion problem `4`'s own `IfcValue` has).
#
# `format u8` + `flags u8` (bit0..3 = `schema`/`header`/non-empty-`removed_instances`/
# non-empty-`upserted_instances` presence, same order the text grammar's token list uses) as two REAL
# fixed fields, then each present field's payload in that order as one trailing `bytes` chain.
# `schema`/`header`/`removed_instances`' own ids and `upserted_instances`' own per-instance fields are
# real field-by-field binary at the Rust layer (`enc_part21_header_bin`/`enc_instance_list_bin` in
# `../../🦀️component.rs`, reusing `store::pack_rt::write_varint_u64`/`store::ByteReader`) — only
# `Part21Value::List`/`Typed`'s self-recursion into `Vec<Part21Value>` cannot be re-modeled
# field-by-field AT THIS DIALECT LAYER, because `Prim::Ref` (the only construct that could describe
# that self-recursion here) unconditionally errors during `walk_protocol`
# (`protocol-prim-ref-recursion`, recipe §5 — confirmed unchanged through every FG-wave pilot, not
# fixed by this wave either). Same honest-boundary treatment the plan prescribes: opaque at the
# protocol layer, genuinely structured (and round-trip-tested) at the Rust layer.
dialect protocol
protocol stdio.ifc.2x3.diff
version 1
schema stdio.ifc.2x3
start record

framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field flags u8
chain payload bytes
